  "id": "COMPOUND:25894 - PROTEIN:6305",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 6-O-Methyl-beta-D-galactopyranose may interact with Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, through its role as a target of multiple compounds. This relationship is supported by the shared target of 6-O-Methyl-beta-D-galactopyranose with DNA polymerase eta, which is itself targeted by compounds such as 2-Oxaisodauc-5-En-12-Al, (2S,3S)-3,3',4',5,7-Pentahydroxy Flavanonol, and Gancaonin P. These compounds all direct their action to Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, indicating a possible pathway where 6-O-Methyl-beta-D-galactopyranose may modulate the activity of DNA polymerase eta, which in turn could influence the function of the vacuolar ATP synthase. The consistent targeting of Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 across these pathways suggests a possible role in cellular energy regulation or other processes dependent on this enzyme. The evidence is supported by a recurring mechanism involving the targeting of DNA polymerase eta, which may serve as a bridge between 6-O-Methyl-beta-D-galactopyranose and the vacuolar ATP synthase. The integration of these findings implies that 6-O-Methyl-beta-D-galactopyranose may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, with the vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 being a key downstream target.",
